IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gst-types`

-- Goods and Services Tax Act 1993 — GOAL 2: MUST THE PERSON REGISTER?
--
--   "Is this person liable to be registered — on the retrospective or the
--    prospective test, as an overseas vendor, or as a reverse charge
--    recipient; by when must it notify; from when is it registered; and when
--    may it leave?"
--
-- Source: ../source/GSTA1993.txt — First Schedule; ss 8(2), 9, 31-34, 91.

§ `Goal 2 — registration`

§§ `Liability to be registered (First Schedule paras 1, 1A, 1B)`

-- Para 1(1)(a)(ii): at the end of a calendar year "if the total value of all
-- ... the person's taxable supplies made in Singapore ... in that calendar year
-- has exceeded $1 million" — unless (3)(b) the Comptroller is satisfied the
-- next year will not exceed $1 million. Para 1(1)(b): "at any time, if there
-- are reasonable grounds for believing that the total value ... in the period
-- of 12 months then beginning will exceed $1 million". Para 1C(2): capital
-- asset supplies are left out (an input); para 16: values exclude tax.
@ref First Schedule para 1(1), (3)(b)
GIVEN r IS A `Registration facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liable to register on the retrospective test` r IF
    r's `taxable supplies in the last calendar year` GREATER THAN 1000000
    AND (NOT r's `Comptroller satisfied next year will not exceed $1 million`)

@ref First Schedule para 1(1)(b)
GIVEN r IS A `Registration facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liable to register on the prospective test` r IF
    r's `taxable supplies expected in the next 12 months` GREATER THAN 1000000

-- Para 1A(1): a person belonging abroad making Seventh Schedule supplies, if
-- "the total value of all the person's taxable supplies, and supplies outside
-- Singapore which would have been taxable supplies if made in Singapore, has
-- exceeded $1 million; and ... the total value of the person's Seventh Schedule
-- supplies has exceeded $100,000" — for the calendar year, or expected in the
-- next 12 months.
@ref First Schedule para 1A(1)
GIVEN r IS A `Registration facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an overseas vendor liable to register` r IF
        (NOT r's `belongs in Singapore`)
    AND (   (r's `global supplies in the last calendar year` GREATER THAN 1000000 AND r's `Seventh Schedule supplies in the last calendar year` GREATER THAN 100000)
         OR (r's `global supplies expected in the next 12 months` GREATER THAN 1000000 AND r's `Seventh Schedule supplies expected in the next 12 months` GREATER THAN 100000))

-- Para 1B(1): a recipient of s 14(1) goods or services, if their value "has
-- exceeded $1 million, and the person is not entitled to credit for the full
-- amount of input tax".
@ref First Schedule para 1B(1)
GIVEN r IS A `Registration facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reverse charge recipient liable to register` r IF
        (NOT r's `entitled to full input tax credit`)
    AND (   r's `reverse charge services received last calendar year` GREATER THAN 1000000
         OR r's `reverse charge services expected in the next 12 months` GREATER THAN 1000000)

@ref First Schedule paras 1, 1A, 1B
GIVEN r IS A `Registration facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liable to be registered` r IF
       `liable to register on the retrospective test` r
    OR `liable to register on the prospective test` r
    OR `an overseas vendor liable to register` r
    OR `a reverse charge recipient liable to register` r

§§ `Notifying and the date of registration (paras 4-6)`

-- Para 4(1A): on the retrospective test, notify "within 30 days after the end
-- of that calendar year"; (2) registered from "the day immediately after the
-- end of the month that follows the month in which the 30th day falls".
@ref First Schedule para 4(1A)-(2)
GIVEN `year ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`must notify the retrospective liability by, year ended` `year ended` MEANS `year ended` PLUS 30

@ref First Schedule para 4(2)
GIVEN `year ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`registered on the retrospective test from, year ended` `year ended` MEANS
    `add months` (Date 1 (DATE_MONTH `the 30th day`) (DATE_YEAR `the 30th day`)) 2
    WHERE
        `the 30th day` MEANS `year ended` PLUS 30

-- Para 5(1): on the prospective test, notify "within 30 days after the first
-- day of that period" (day X). (2)(a)(ii): where day X is on or after 1 July
-- 2025, registered from "the day in the second month (month M + 2) following
-- the month (month M) in which day X falls, that corresponds numerically to day
-- X" — or the last day of month M + 2 if there is none; (2)(a)(i): before
-- 1 July 2025, the day after the 30 days.
@ref First Schedule para 5(1)
GIVEN `day X` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`must notify the prospective liability by, day X` `day X` MEANS `day X` PLUS 30

@ref First Schedule para 5(2)(a)
GIVEN `day X` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`registered on the prospective test from, day X` `day X` MEANS
    IF `day X` AT LEAST YMD 2025 7 1
    THEN `add months` `day X` 2
    ELSE `day X` PLUS 31

-- Para 6: on a transfer of a going concern, notify within 30 days and register
-- "with effect from the day on which the business is transferred". Para 4(5),
-- 5(2C), 6(5): a later registration after a refusal not earlier than 30 days
-- after notice.
@ref First Schedule para 6(1)-(2)
GIVEN transferred IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`must notify a transfer liability by, transferred` transferred MEANS transferred PLUS 30

@ref First Schedule paras 4(5)(b), 5(2C)(b), 6(5)(b)
GIVEN notified IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`a deferred registration may take effect no earlier than, notified` notified MEANS notified PLUS 30

-- Para 1A(5), 10, 11, 15(2)-(3), 17(4): changes notified "within 30 days".
@ref First Schedule paras 1A(5), 10, 11, 15(2)-(3), 17(4)
GIVEN event IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`a change must be notified by, event` event MEANS event PLUS 30

§§ `Leaving the register (paras 3, 8, 12-14)`

-- Para 3: liability ends if in the next 12 months taxable supplies "will not
-- exceed $1 million", for a reason other than ceasing or suspending supplies
-- for 30 days or more.
@ref First Schedule para 3
GIVEN `expected next 12 months` IS A NUMBER, `because supplies cease or pause 30 days or more` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liability to be registered ends, expected` `expected next 12 months` `, ceasing or pausing:` `because supplies cease or pause 30 days or more` IF
    `expected next 12 months` AT MOST 1000000 AND (NOT `because supplies cease or pause 30 days or more`)

-- Para 8(2): a voluntary registration lasts "not less than 2 years or such
-- other shorter period as the Comptroller may determine".
@ref First Schedule para 8(2)
GIVEN registered IS A DATE, `shorter period allowed until` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`a voluntary registration lasts at least until, registered` registered `, shorter period` `shorter period allowed until` MEANS
    CONSIDER `shorter period allowed until`
    WHEN JUST d  THEN d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add years` registered 2

-- Para 8(1): voluntary registration if the person makes taxable supplies (or
-- qualifying exempt international supplies), intends to in a business, is an
-- overseas Seventh Schedule supplier, or is a s 14(1) recipient.
@ref First Schedule para 8(1)
GIVEN `makes or intends taxable or qualifying supplies` IS A BOOLEAN, `an overseas Seventh Schedule supplier or s 14(1) recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may register voluntarily, supplies:` `makes or intends taxable or qualifying supplies` `, overseas or recipient:` `an overseas Seventh Schedule supplier or s 14(1) recipient` IF
    `makes or intends taxable or qualifying supplies` OR `an overseas Seventh Schedule supplier or s 14(1) recipient`

§§ `Who registers and who is liable (ss 31-34)`

-- s 31(3): until a change in a partnership is notified in writing, a
-- departing partner "is regarded as continuing to be a partner". s 31(7): a
-- part-period partner's share is "such proportion ... as may be just".
@ref s 31(3)
GIVEN `change notified in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the former partner is still liable as a partner, change notified:` `change notified in writing` IF
    NOT `change notified in writing`

-- s 32(6): a person carrying on a dead, insolvent or incapacitated person's
-- business must inform the Comptroller "within 21 days after commencing".
@ref s 32(6)
GIVEN commenced IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`must inform the Comptroller of carrying on the business by, commenced` commenced MEANS commenced PLUS 21

-- s 33(1): an overseas registrant "must" appoint a section 33(1) agent unless
-- it is a pay-only Seventh Schedule registrant, which "may"; (1B)(b) notify
-- "not more than 30 days after" appointment; (1B)(c) a change "not less than
-- 30 days before".
@ref s 33(1), (1B)-(1C)
GIVEN `usual residence in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `a pay-only Seventh Schedule registrant` IS A BOOLEAN, `waived by the Comptroller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must appoint a section 33(1) agent, resident:` `usual residence in Singapore` `, pay-only:` `a pay-only Seventh Schedule registrant` `, waived:` `waived by the Comptroller` IF
    (NOT `usual residence in Singapore`) AND (NOT `a pay-only Seventh Schedule registrant`) AND (NOT `waived by the Comptroller`)

-- s 30(2): group members "shall be liable jointly and severally for any tax due
-- from the representative member"; s 30(1)(a): intra-group supplies are
-- disregarded, but (1A) not a reverse charge supply.
@ref s 30(1)(a), (1A)
GIVEN `between group members` IS A BOOLEAN, `would give rise to a reverse charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supply is disregarded, intra-group:` `between group members` `, reverse charge:` `would give rise to a reverse charge` IF
    `between group members` AND (NOT `would give rise to a reverse charge`)

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 9, 28, 28A, 29, 30(2)-(4), 31(1)-(2), (4)-(8), 32(1)-(5), 33(1A), (1D)-(5), 33AA, 33A, 33B, 34, 34A, 91; First Schedule paras 1(2), (3A)-(4), 1A(2)-(4), 1B(2), 1C, 2, 3A-3C, 4(3)-(4), 5(2A)-(4), 6(3)-(4), 7, 7A, 9, 12-14A, 15(1)-(1A), 16-19
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`registration provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "ss 28-29: public agencies; pay-only overseas registrants; deemed input tax on insurance payments"
         "ss 30-33AA: groups, partnerships, divisions, clubs, trusts, umbrella VCCs and sub-funds, agents and section 33(1) agents"
         "ss 33A-34A: refunds to overseas businesses, processed imports, transfers of going concerns"
         "s 91: the 2019 and 2022 transitional registrations"
         "First Schedule: going-concern transferees, VCC mergers, Comptroller's aggregation directions, the end of liability for overseas vendors and recipients, refusal, conditions, cancellation, exemption for zero-rated suppliers, forms and the register"
